1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,308
F S L maths and F S L means.

2
00:00:03,308 --> 00:00:08,455
Create masks and extract a mean time series without losing track of image space.

3
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:11,763
The goal is clear: Build a simple thresholded mask.

4
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:14,320
Transform first, measure second.

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:20,294
F S L maths applies image operations in sequence and writes a new image.

6
00:00:20,294 --> 00:00:25,415
F S L means summarizes a four-D time series within a mask.

7
00:00:25,415 --> 00:00:30,536
The mask and source data must have compatible dimensions and spatial alignment.

8
00:00:30,536 --> 00:00:35,229
A binary mask contains 1 for included voxels and 0 elsewhere.

9
00:00:35,229 --> 00:00:41,204
Thresholding alone may not create a scientifically valid ROI; it is simply an operation.

10
00:00:41,204 --> 00:00:45,471
View every derived mask before using it to extract values.

11
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:49,504
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

12
00:00:49,504 --> 00:00:53,084
First, create a binary mask from an example image.

13
00:00:53,084 --> 00:00:56,267
Next, open the mask over the source image.

14
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:59,450
Then, confirm dimensions with F S L info.

15
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:04,224
After that, extract a mean time series and inspect its first values.

16
00:01:04,224 --> 00:01:07,406
The command shown on screen is an example.

17
00:01:07,406 --> 00:01:13,374
Adapt its path to your own working directory and verify the target before running it.

18
00:01:14,224 --> 00:01:15,440
Quality Control Check.

19
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,491
Overlay the mask on the exact image used for extraction.

20
00:01:19,491 --> 00:01:22,733
Matching dimensions do not guarantee meaningful anatomical alignment.

21
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:30,026
A useful self-check is this: What must you verify before using a mask with F S L means?

22
00:01:30,026 --> 00:01:36,915
That it is scientifically appropriate and aligned to the same dimensions and space as the four-D input.

23
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:44,112
To recap: First, F S L maths writes derived images; preserve meaningful names.

24
00:01:44,112 --> 00:01:48,506
Next, never extract a signal from an uninspected mask.

25
00:01:48,506 --> 00:01:55,342
Before continuing, make sure you can explain this objective: Build a simple thresholded mask.
